### US3 Acceptance Tests
### User Story 3: 已登入使用者可發文並管理自己的貼文

# Test environment
@baseUrl = http://localhost/api
@user1Phone = +886901234501
@user1Pass = Pass1234
@user2Phone = +886901234502
@user2Pass = Pass2234

### Step 1: Register user1 (Author A)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phoneNumber": "{{user1Phone}}",
  "userName": "TestUser1",
  "password": "{{user1Pass}}"
}

### Step 2: Login user1
# @name loginUser1
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phoneNumber": "{{user1Phone}}",
  "password": "{{user1Pass}}"
}

### Capture user1 token
@user1Token = {{loginUser1.response.body.accessToken}}

### Step 3: Register user2 (User B who will try to edit/delete)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phoneNumber": "{{user2Phone}}",
  "userName": "TestUser2",
  "password": "{{user2Pass}}"
}

### Step 4: Login user2
# @name loginUser2
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phoneNumber": "{{user2Phone}}",
  "password": "{{user2Pass}}"
}

### Capture user2 token
@user2Token = {{loginUser2.response.body.accessToken}}

### Step 5: User1 creates a post
# @name createPost
POST {{baseUrl}}/posts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

{
  "content": "This is a test post from User1",
  "image": "https://example.com/image.jpg"
}

### Capture postId
@postId = {{createPost.response.body.postId}}

### Step 6: Verify post appears in list
GET {{baseUrl}}/posts?limit=20&offset=0

### Step 7: User2 tries to update User1's post (should get 403)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{postId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{user2Token}}

{
  "content": "User2 trying to edit User1's post"
}

### Expected: 403 Forbidden

### Step 8: User2 tries to delete User1's post (should get 403)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{postId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{user2Token}}

### Expected: 403 Forbidden

### Step 9: User1 updates their own post (should succeed)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{postId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

{
  "content": "Updated content by User1"
}

### Expected: 200 OK with updated post

### Step 10: User1 updates post with partial data (only image)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{postId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

{
  "image": "https://example.com/new-image.jpg"
}

### Expected: 200 OK, content unchanged, image updated

### Step 11: Verify post is updated in list
GET {{baseUrl}}/posts?limit=20&offset=0

### Step 12: User1 soft deletes their own post (should succeed)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{postId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

### Expected: 204 No Content

### Step 13: Verify deleted post doesn't appear in list
GET {{baseUrl}}/posts?limit=20&offset=0

### Step 14: Try to delete already deleted post (should get 404)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{postId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

### Expected: 404 Not Found

### Step 15: Try to update deleted post (should get 404)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/posts/{{postId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

{
  "content": "Trying to update deleted post"
}

### Expected: 404 Not Found

### Step 16: Create post without auth (should get 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/posts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "Unauthenticated post attempt"
}

### Expected: 401 Unauthorized

### Step 17: Create post with empty content (should get 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/posts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

{
  "content": "   "
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request

### Step 18: Create post with invalid image URL (should get 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/posts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

{
  "content": "Test post",
  "image": "not-a-url"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request

### Step 19: Create post with image URL too long (should get 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/posts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

{
  "content": "Test post",
  "image": "https://example..jpg"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request

### Step 20: Test successful post creation with valid data
# @name createValidPost
POST {{baseUrl}}/posts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

{
  "content": "Valid post content",
  "image": "https://example.com/valid-image.jpg"
}

### Expected: 201 Created with post data

### Step 21: Create post without image (optional field)
POST {{baseUrl}}/posts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

{
  "content": "Post without image"
}

### Expected: 201 Created

###

### Step 22: Update post with invalid postId format (should get 400)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/posts/invalid-uuid-format
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

{
  "content": "Trying to update with invalid ID"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request - Invalid post ID format

###

### Step 23: Delete post with invalid postId format (should get 400)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/posts/not-a-valid-uuid
Authorization: Bearer {{user1Token}}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request - Invalid post ID format
